/T (The objective of treatment for OCD is to weaken the fearful associations held by an individual through self-initiated contact with the situations or circumstances that trigger emotional distress, while discouraging the use of unhealthy behavioural responses that keep the cycle of obsession in motion. Referred to as exposure, this self-initiated contact is most effective when designed to trigger a tolerable amount of distress before moving onto challenges that bring about a greater degree of anxiety. When exposures are organised and tackled from least anxiety-provoking to most anxiety-provoking, individuals are more likely to experience a gradual reduction of their anxiety in relation to intrusive thoughts.)
/E (The objective of treatment for OCD is to weaken the fearful associations held by an individual through self-initiated contact with the situations or circumstances that trigger emotional distress, while discouraging the use of unhealthy behavioural responses that keep the cycle of obsession in motion. Referred to as exposure, this self-initiated contact is most effective when designed to trigger a tolerable amount of distress before moving onto challenges that bring about a greater degree of anxiety. When exposures are organised and tackled from least anxiety-provoking to most anxiety-provoking, individuals are more likely to experience a gradual reduction of their anxiety in relation to intrusive thoughts.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
