/T (Serotonin \(5-HT\): Serotonin is perhaps the most extensively studied neurotransmitter in the context of OCD. Evidence suggests that dysregulation of the serotonin system, particularly reduced levels of serotonin, is associated with the pathophysiology of OCD \(Albert et al., 2020\). Selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors \(SSRIs\), which increase serotonin levels in the brain, are commonly used as first-line pharmacological treatments for OCD, further supporting the serotonin hypothesis of OCD.)
/E (Serotonin \(5-HT\): Serotonin is perhaps the most extensively studied neurotransmitter in the context of OCD. Evidence suggests that dysregulation of the serotonin system, particularly reduced levels of serotonin, is associated with the pathophysiology of OCD \(Albert et al., 2020\). Selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors \(SSRIs\), which increase serotonin levels in the brain, are commonly used as first-line pharmacological treatments for OCD, further supporting the serotonin hypothesis of OCD.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [12]
