/E (Glutamate: Glutamate is the primary excitatory neurotransmitter in the brain and has been implicated in the neurobiology of OCD. Dysfunctions in glutamatergic neurotransmission, specifically abnormalities in glutamate levels or receptor functioning, have been observed in individuals with OCD \(Fineberg et al., 2020\). Emerging research suggests that targeting the glutamatergic system may offer novel therapeutic avenues for the treatment of OCD.)
