/E (B-vitamins, a group of water-soluble vitamins that play essential roles in cellular metabolism and neurological function, have garnered attention in recent years for their potential implications in mental health disorders, including Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder \(OCD\). Studies suggest that deficiencies in certain B-vitamins may contribute to alterations in neurotransmitter function and neuronal pathways implicated in OCD symptomatology.)
