/S /H3
/P 196 0 R
/T (Vitamin B6 \(Pyridoxine\): Vitamin B6 is involved in the synthesis of neurotransmitters such as serotonin, dopamine, and gamma-aminobutyric acid \(GABA\), which play critical roles in mood regulation and anxiety modulation, both of which are central to OCD pathology \(Fernstrom, 2012\). Research indicates that inadequate levels of vitamin B6 may disrupt neurotransmitter balance, potentially exacerbating symptoms of OCD \(Sarris et al., 2012\).)
/E (Vitamin B6 \(Pyridoxine\): Vitamin B6 is involved in the synthesis of neurotransmitters such as serotonin, dopamine, and gamma-aminobutyric acid \(GABA\), which play critical roles in mood regulation and anxiety modulation, both of which are central to OCD pathology \(Fernstrom, 2012\). Research indicates that inadequate levels of vitamin B6 may disrupt neurotransmitter balance, potentially exacerbating symptoms of OCD \(Sarris et al., 2012\).)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
