327 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 196 0 R
/T (Vitamin B12 \(Cobalamin\): Vitamin B12 is essential for the maintenance of neuronal integrity and the synthesis of myelin, the protective sheath surrounding nerve fibers. Deficiencies in vitamin B12 have been linked to neurological symptoms such as cognitive impairment and mood disturbances, which may exacerbate OCD symptoms \(Hutto, 2008\). Furthermore, vitamin B12 plays a role in the methylation cycle, which regulates neurotransmitter metabolism, suggesting a potential mechanism by which its deficiency could impact OCD pathology \(Bottiglieri et al., 2000\).)
/E (Vitamin B12 \(Cobalamin\): Vitamin B12 is essential for the maintenance of neuronal integrity and the synthesis of myelin, the protective sheath surrounding nerve fibers. Deficiencies in vitamin B12 have been linked to neurological symptoms such as cognitive impairment and mood disturbances, which may exacerbate OCD symptoms \(Hutto, 2008\). Furthermore, vitamin B12 plays a role in the methylation cycle, which regulates neurotransmitter metabolism, suggesting a potential mechanism by which its deficiency could impact OCD pathology \(Bottiglieri et al., 2000\).)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
