/T (Methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase \(MTHFR\) is a crucial enzyme involved in the methylation cycle, which regulates various biochemical processes, including neurotransmitter synthesis and DNA methylation. Genetic variations in the MTHFR gene, particularly the C677T and A1298C polymorphisms, have been associated with reduced enzyme activity and impaired folate metabolism, potentially contributing to alterations in neurotransmitter function and increased susceptibility to mental health disorders, including OCD.)
/E (Methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase \(MTHFR\) is a crucial enzyme involved in the methylation cycle, which regulates various biochemical processes, including neurotransmitter synthesis and DNA methylation. Genetic variations in the MTHFR gene, particularly the C677T and A1298C polymorphisms, have been associated with reduced enzyme activity and impaired folate metabolism, potentially contributing to alterations in neurotransmitter function and increased susceptibility to mental health disorders, including OCD.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
