/T (Several studies have investigated the relationship between MTHFR gene mutations and OCD, with some suggesting a potential link between MTHFR polymorphisms and increased susceptibility to OCD symptoms. For example, a meta-analysis by Liu et al. \(2018\) found that individuals with the MTHFR C677T polymorphism may have a higher risk of developing OCD, particularly in certain ethnic populations.)
/E (Several studies have investigated the relationship between MTHFR gene mutations and OCD, with some suggesting a potential link between MTHFR polymorphisms and increased susceptibility to OCD symptoms. For example, a meta-analysis by Liu et al. \(2018\) found that individuals with the MTHFR C677T polymorphism may have a higher risk of developing OCD, particularly in certain ethnic populations.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [13]
