/P 203 0 R
/T (Due to the 'mechanistic' nature of OCD partly arising from a malfunctioning neurological circuit, treatment, therefore, should be systematic and behaviour-based. Contrary to traditional Cognitive Behaviour Therapy \(CBT\) approaches, which seek to challenge irrational thinking by weighing the evidence and plausibility of specific thoughts, successful OCD treatment more closely resembles basic mindfulness practices by way of noticing  thoughts, be they rational or irrational, without directly engaging with or attempting to change them.)
/E (Due to the 'mechanistic' nature of OCD partly arising from a malfunctioning neurological circuit, treatment, therefore, should be systematic and behaviour-based. Contrary to traditional Cognitive Behaviour Therapy \(CBT\) approaches, which seek to challenge irrational thinking by weighing the evidence and plausibility of specific thoughts, successful OCD treatment more closely resembles basic mindfulness practices by way of noticing  thoughts, be they rational or irrational, without directly engaging with or attempting to change them.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
462 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
