/T (ERP is predicated on the process of habituation, which refers to the brains ability to habituate, or reduce its response to, a particular situation, circumstance or thought after repeated exposures or contact. In the context of OCD, habituation occurs when the brain gradually learns to no longer fear an obsessional theme as a result of voluntary contact with it.  This contact, referred to as an exposure, provides the brain with   )
/E (ERP is predicated on the process of habituation, which refers to the brains ability to habituate, or reduce its response to, a particular situation, circumstance or thought after repeated exposures or contact. In the context of OCD, habituation occurs when the brain gradually learns to no longer fear an obsessional theme as a result of voluntary contact with it.  This contact, referred to as an exposure, provides the brain with   )
/Pg 27 0 R
