/E (This is reflected in our neurology, too, with our prefrontal cortex \(front of the brain\) acting as the seat of this observing self. While various other brain structures relay messages to the observer self by way of thoughts, sensations and emotions,  it is the observer self's job to decide which of these messages are valid, and which are unworthy of our precious energy and attention. Obsessive thoughts, while intrusive and uncomfortable, are merely another 'message' sent to us from our brains.)
