/E (We get into trouble when we start to demonise a particular message as horrible, unacceptable or somehow reflective of our 'true selves', which is how particular thoughts become paired so strongly with overwhelming anxiety. Essentially, our task in therapy is to 'reverse engineer' this process of labelling particular thoughts as unacceptably bad, and to instead treat all thoughts, whether intrusive or not, as neutral fragments of information that we are free to entertain or ignore.)
