/T (To illustrate the point further, imagine you are the CEO \(observer self\) of a company \(your brain\). The CEO's job is take in all available information from within the company, and to decide on how the company will spend it's resources, solve problems and maximise profits. Advisors, managers and employees \(brain messages\) meet regularly with the CEO to report said information, and to offer insights as to the wellbeing of the company. However, the CEO is free to take the offered information or to reject it. The same goes for your brain and the thoughts it likes to gives you. You are free to take on thoughts, feelings and sensations as  your identity, or you are free to practice defusion.)
/E (To illustrate the point further, imagine you are the CEO \(observer self\) of a company \(your brain\). The CEO's job is take in all available information from within the company, and to decide on how the company will spend it's resources, solve problems and maximise profits. Advisors, managers and employees \(brain messages\) meet regularly with the CEO to report said information, and to offer insights as to the wellbeing of the company. However, the CEO is free to take the offered information or to reject it. The same goes for your brain and the thoughts it likes to gives you. You are free to take on thoughts, feelings and sensations as  your identity, or you are free to practice defusion.)
