/P 217 0 R
/T (She steps up the challenge and reduces her available compulsion tokens further by one and repeats the process until she is no longer using any compulsion tokens in the face of intrusive thoughts. Eventually, she does the same for her other compulsions, although she discovers she needs to go much slower, as these compulsions are a little more entrenched.)
/E (She steps up the challenge and reduces her available compulsion tokens further by one and repeats the process until she is no longer using any compulsion tokens in the face of intrusive thoughts. Eventually, she does the same for her other compulsions, although she discovers she needs to go much slower, as these compulsions are a little more entrenched.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
683 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 217 0 R
/T (Compulsion reduction strategy: compulsion tokens)
/E (Compulsion reduction strategy: compulsion tokens)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
684 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 217 0 R
/T (Because recovery from OCD is a gradual and challenging process, we need to progress at a steady, but slow rate. Utilising compulsion tokens is a very effective way of gradually reducing reliance on safety behaviours and avoidance of anxiety simultaneously. The beauty of this approach is that you are in control of how fast or slow you travel.)
/E (Because recovery from OCD is a gradual and challenging process, we need to progress at a steady, but slow rate. Utilising compulsion tokens is a very effective way of gradually reducing reliance on safety behaviours and avoidance of anxiety simultaneously. The beauty of this approach is that you are in control of how fast or slow you travel.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
