714 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 220 0 R
/E (You have made to the end of the Self-Therapy Guidebook for OCD! This is no small feat, as challenging our habits, some of which have been lifelong, is an arduous and exhausting process, but one that is ultimately rewarding and inspiring. While this guidebook was intended to be read from start to finish as a simulation of a course of therapy administered by a professional, it is highly recommended that you return to any section of the content as needed to maintain upkeep of your emerging recovery skillset.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
715 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 220 0 R
/E (As a final note, any process of personal change is hard, and requires reserves of willpower, disciplined action, and a clear goal or 'why' for undertaking it. Mental health, like anything else, is largely a composite of healthy micro-behaviours conspiring to improve your overall quality of life, so take it slow, and steadily build the behaviours necessary to facilitate this process.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
716 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 220 0 R
/E (Once again, congratulations for taking steps forward to improve your life, and we wish you the very best on the road to recovery from OCD.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
