2076 0 obj
<<
/Title (Why can't I stop!?)
/Dest [40 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2084 0 R
/Next 2072 0 R
>>
endobj
2077 0 obj
<<
/Title (Firstly, you absolutely can stop - this I can confidently assure you of. As we've outlined in previous modules, you brain has paired the compulsion, regardless of what kind you use, with relief. Relief from pain, be it physical or emotional pain, is a powerful reinforcer for behaviour, which is, in some ways, how addiction can start. You can think of compulsions as an addiction of sorts, as the rush of relief floods your nervous system with a wave of the reward-hormone dopamine. This same hormone is released when we anticipate a reward, consume drugs or alcohol, and achieve a goal or objective.)
/Dest [40 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2072 0 R
/Next 2078 0 R
>>
endobj
2078 0 obj
<<
/Title (Naturally, our brains like to feel good, so the next time it kicks off the OCD cycle with an intrusive brain message, you can almost view as your brain's way of attempting to get its next 'hit', so to speak. Pair the metaphor for addiction with the fear of anxiety, and you have a pretty good explanation for why you feel you can't stop.)
/Dest [40 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2072 0 R
/Prev 2077 0 R
>>
endobj
2079 0 obj
<<
/Title (Let's put this in the context of an example:)
/Dest [40 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2069 0 R
/Prev 2073 0 R
/Next 2085 0 R
>>
endobj
2080 0 obj
<<
/Title (She scans the compulsion counter resource \(pg. \) and inputs the number of times she's permitted to perform the compulsion for the next day. When she has used up all her tokens, she commits to feeling the anxiety associated with the intrusive thought that she's experiencing bodily symptoms of AIDS, and to deny herself the urge to give into the compulsion. She instead sits with the anxiety and waits for it to peak and then trough \(see the anxiety curve on page 10\). After a few days of repeating this process, she notices that there is substantially less anxiety when she's out of compulsion tokens as compared to previous days.)
/Dest [40 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2069 0 R
/Prev 2086 0 R
/Next 2074 0 R
>>
