2104 0 obj
<<
/Title (to struggle within a seemingly endless mental prison. For example, some individuals with OCD will ruminate tirelessly on the question of whether they wish to harm their family and closest friends, and experience extreme anxiety at the prospect that these thoughts may be indicative of a genuine desire. This sub variant of OCD, known as Harm-OCD, is one of many examples of a lesser known type of the disorder called Pure-Obsessional OCD, or Pure-O. Pure-O is mechanically identically to classic OCD presentations, although the compulsions used to counteract anxiety \(see below\) are almost entirely mental.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2089 0 R
/Prev 2103 0 R
/Next 2097 0 R
>>
endobj
2105 0 obj
<<
/Title (The objective of treatment for OCD is to weaken the fearful associations held by an individual through self-initiated contact with the situations or circumstances that trigger emotional distress, while discouraging the use of unhealthy behavioural responses that keep the cycle of obsession in motion. Referred to as exposure, this self-initiated contact is most effective when designed to trigger a tolerable amount of distress before moving onto challenges that bring about a greater degree of anxiety. When exposures are organised and tackled from least anxiety-provoking to most anxiety-provoking, individuals are more likely to experience a gradual reduction of their anxiety in relation to intrusive thoughts.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2083 0 R
/Prev 2098 0 R
/Next 2106 0 R
>>
endobj
2106 0 obj
<<
/Title (Like all diagnoses, figuring out how OCD manifests is complex, and there are usually a number of factors contributing to its development. Researchers have indicated the high probability of genetics playing a key role, with the identification of several potentially relevant genes, but studies have also concluded that more research is required. Environmental factors can also influence the likelihood of OCD symptom development as early experiences with anxiety and the behaviours used to successfully reduce distress may lay the foundation for future OCD-type patterns.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2083 0 R
/Prev 2105 0 R
/Next 2099 0 R
>>
endobj
