2111 0 obj
<<
/Title (This activation may then lead to obsessional fixation on the material emerging into consciousness as a result of this malfunctioning circuitry. Moreover, this excitatory pathway appears to operate as a positive feedback loop, meaning that obsessions or signals of danger increase in magnitude over time. It also appears to be the case that for OCD brains the inhibitory pathway, which reduces signals of danger, is less effective, which may explain how and why intrusive thoughts are generated.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
