2113 0 obj
<<
/Title (Dogmatic thinking, which is the rigid adherence to an ideal or position despite evidence to the contrary, is undoubtedly dangerous. Proponents of the idea that mental health can simply be reduced to an 'imbalance' to one or more neurotransmitters are likely oversimplifying the problem , and may \(read: definitely do!\) have vested interests in doing so \(cha-ching!\). While the chemical \(monoamine\) hypothesis has come under fire recently with the publishing of a review concluding there to be no link between depression and serotonin levels \(University College of London, 2022\), I believe it is equally as irresponsible to conclude that neurotransmitters have ZERO association with mental health.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2109 0 R
/Next 2117 0 R
>>
endobj
