/Title (As we've learned, compulsions are the 'fuel' maintaining the cycle of OCD. If you can can imagine the OCD cycle as a snarling beast, then our ritualised behaviours aimed at reducing our emotional distress are it's sustenance. Without it, it starves and eventually dies. This is why so much of the therapeutic process for OCD is about reducing compulsions, and ultimately learning to better tolerate the anxiety that undoubtedly arises when we stop running from it.)
/Dest [38 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2218 0 R
