<<
/Title (Brains learn by experience, and, interestingly, this experience does not have to be derived from physical engagement with our environment. So, if we experience anxiety following an intrusive thought and we jump immediately into a compulsion, the brain's 'experience' in that moment is the intrusive thought is dangerous and says something horrible about me, when, in actual fact, this is simply not the case. Recovery from OCD is allowing your brain the healthy experience of learning)
