2231 0 obj
<<
/Title (In-vivo, or in-person, exposures are exposure exercises in which an individual physically engages with a situation, circumstance or object that prompts intrusive thoughts while abstaining from any safety behaviours used to mitigate anxiety. Examples of in-vivo exposures include steadily increasing contact with a feared location, such as a public toilet, due to obsessive contamination concerns. In this situation, an individual with this particular obsession might first be instructed to look at pictures of public toilets followed by videos of stalls. Next, they would be encouraged to visit one at a distance, while steadily closing the gap between themselves and the cubicle or stall. Eventually someone with this obsession might even use a public toilet as their 'worst-case scenario' or most feared situation, and once they are able to use a public toilet enough times without engaging in compulsions or experiencing overwhelming anxiety, they would have largely 'extinguished' or recovered from their OCD symptoms.)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2222 0 R
>>
endobj
2232 0 obj
<<
