/Title (Imaginal exposures are highly effective for individuals with obsessions that are not directly accessible throughout everyday life. For example, if someone experiences existential intrusive thoughts regarding whether or not they actually exist, attempting to design an in-person exposure is nigh on impossible. To remedy this, the imaginal exposure can provide a means for the individual to directly face more philosophical-oriented obsessions. Moreover, if someone is stricken with the obsession that they are not the sexual orientation they've always known themselves to be \(sexual orientation OCD\), imaginal exposures can serve to challenge intrusive thoughts in a discrete and effective way. It should be stated that some obsessional themes, like sexual orientation OCD, can benefit from a combined imaginal and in-person exposure program.)
/Dest [27 0 R /Fit]
