2301 0 obj
<<
/Title (In essence, a backdoor spike is the brain's way of attempting to return to 'normalcy', which is the OCD cycle. A really important fact about human nature, and our brains, is that consistency is sought out above all, even above relief from suffering. This is how and why we can get stuck inside all sorts of unhealthy and maladaptive patterns despite 'knowing' or, perhaps on the surface, wanting for things to change. This is core of resistance, which is simply the brain's desire to remain as is for the sake of convenience and predictability. Pair this with OCD's refusal to tolerate uncertainty, and you have a recipe for an onslaught of backdoor spikes.)
/Dest [34 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2269 0 R
/Prev 2286 0 R
/Next 2287 0 R
>>
endobj
