/Title (What we're actually doing by thanking our brain is acknowledging that a particular thought has made it's way to our observer self without seeking to explore, analyse, ruminate on or change it. It is precisely these and other follow-up behaviours \(compulsions\) that feed the cycle of OCD. By accepting the presence, and not the premise, we're free to focus our attention elsewhere, which will likely result in the intrusive thought receding away from awareness once more.)
