2346 0 obj
<<
/Title (Having high distress tolerance does not mean that you do not experience anxiety, but rather  when you do, you're able to remain in your observer self, so as to maintain good judgement and decision making skills. It means that your chosen life-path is unaltered by the presence of emotional discomfort. Building distress tolerance throughout OCD recovery is essential, and works much like a muscle in the gym. It takes time to build up, and you always need to apply the right amount of 'stress' to the muscle in order for it to grow. Too much and the muscle won't be able to lift the weight to train. Too little and you won't be stimulating the muscle anywhere near enough. Finding the right amount of discomfort will help you to grow.)
/Dest [33 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2325 0 R
/Prev 2341 0 R
/Next 2342 0 R
>>
endobj
